From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Wed, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: sunxi: enable regulator-always-on / regulator-boot-on regulators

U-Boot's driver model probes devices lazily, so regulators marked
regulator-always-on / regulator-boot-on in the DT are only ever enabled
if something happens to probe them. rockchip, exynos, stm32mp1, amlogic
and veyron board init all call regulators_enable_boot_on() for exactly
this reason - sunxi did not, so on Recore the DT properties silently did
nothing.

The USB VBUS rails were instead being powered by "regulator status" in
CONFIG_PREBOOT, which probes every regulator as a side effect. That ran
milliseconds before "usb reset", leaving devices no time to warm up, and
cost roughly half of all boots a USB device during enumeration with
"EHCI timed out on TD" (intelligent-agent/Reflash#88).

Enabling them here instead - much earlier in boot - fixes that: 20/20
clean boots versus a ~50% failure rate before.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <axp_pmic.h>
 #include <generic-phy.h>
 #include <phy-sun4i-usb.h>
+#include <power/regulator.h>
 #include <asm/arch/clock.h>
 #include <asm/arch/cpu.h>
 #include <asm/arch/display.h>
@@ -244,6 +245,36 @@
 #endif
 	eth_init_board();
 
+#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(DM_REGULATOR)
+	/*
+	 * Enable regulators marked regulator-always-on / regulator-boot-on
+	 * in the device tree.
+	 *
+	 * Unlike Linux, U-Boot's driver model probes devices lazily - only
+	 * when something asks for them. Those two properties are acted on
+	 * in regulator_autoset(), which runs at probe time, so on a board
+	 * where nothing references a regulator it is simply never enabled
+	 * and the DT properties silently do nothing. rockchip, exynos,
+	 * stm32mp1, amlogic and veyron board init all call this for that
+	 * reason; sunxi was the odd one out.
+	 *
+	 * Boards that worked around this by putting "regulator status" in
+	 * CONFIG_PREBOOT (it probes every regulator as a documented side
+	 * effect) can drop it once this is in place.
+	 *
+	 * On Recore this also fixes intermittent USB enumeration failures.
+	 * The six USB VBUS rails used to come up from that PREBOOT command
+	 * milliseconds before "usb reset" ran, leaving devices no time to
+	 * warm up; roughly half of all boots lost a device with
+	 * "EHCI timed out on TD" during the bus scan. Enabling them here
+	 * instead - much earlier in boot - gives them time to settle:
+	 * 20/20 clean boots afterwards versus a ~50% failure rate before.
+	 */
+	ret = regulators_enable_boot_on(false);
+	if (ret)
+		debug("%s: Cannot enable boot on regulators\n", __func__);
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
